          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tuff Duck is a water-based acrylic from Rocklinite Labs that is easy to apply, looks good and beads water well when fresh. It is a thin film, so it wears first where a kitchen works hardest, and the listing's food-safe claim comes without a named certification behind it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy it for a vanity, a hearth or a first DIY countertop where recoating is no hardship. For a busy cooking kitchen, a water-based polyurethane from our countertop sealer guide is the better long-term choice. Whichever you choose, the slab's cure, the prep and thin coats matter more than the brand.
